The article describes a two-environment CI/CD pipeline:

Staging environment

Production environment

Branches:

staging
main
3️⃣ Correct Flow Explained
Step 1 — Developer pushes code
Developer
   │
   ▼
Push → staging branch

Command example:

git push origin staging
Step 2 — GitHub Actions runs CI

Workflow runs when staging branch updates.

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - staging

GitHub will:

1️⃣ Install dependencies
2️⃣ Run tests
3️⃣ Check code quality
4️⃣ Deploy to staging server

Flow:

Push → staging
      │
      ▼
GitHub Actions
      │
      ▼
CI tests
      │
      ▼
Deploy to staging server

Now the module runs on a staging Odoo server.

4️⃣ Step 3 — Manager Reviews Changes

Manager tests the system on staging.

Example checks:

module installs

UI works

no errors

business logic correct

If everything looks good → they approve.

5️⃣ Step 4 — Pull Request to Production

Now the developer creates a Pull Request:

staging → main

In GitHub:

New Pull Request
base: main
compare: staging

Manager reviews the PR and clicks:

Merge Pull Request
6️⃣ Step 5 — Production Deployment

When code merges into main:

Another GitHub Actions workflow runs.

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

Now deployment happens on production server.

Flow:

Merge PR → main
      │
      ▼
GitHub Actions
      │
      ▼
Deploy to Production Odoo Server
